  "notes": "Synthetic Gen2 mechanic vectors for Lua/JS BattleSim2 parity. No ROM data: no species, move, ability or item names — only integer ids and type indices. All arithmetic is integer. DAMAGE (engine src/battle/gen2/Damage.lua): no 255-stat clamp. levelTerm = floor(2L/5)+2 (crit does NOT double L). base = floor(floor(levelTerm*power*attack/defense)/50). Then optional item boost, crit x2, then min(d,997)+2. STAB floor(d*15/10). Type effectiveness is a list of percents applied one at a time as floor(d*pct/100) with a non-immune floor of 1. Variation last: when modified>=2, damage=max(1,min(999,floor(d*roll/100))) for roll in 85..100. Physical reads attack/atk; special (physical:false) reads spa (legacy spc) vs spd (legacy spc). CRIT: ladder 1-in-{15,8,4,3,2,2,2} by critical level 0..6; isCrit when roll==0 for roll in 0..chance-1. Level += focusEnergy(+1), highCritMove(+2), scopeLens(+1), speciesItemBonus(+2), capped at 6. ACCURACY: percent domain; accuracy 0 or alwaysHits never misses; else value=stage-scaled accuracy clamped 1..100, hit = roll < value for roll in 0..99 (no Gen1 1/256 miss). STATUS: freeze thaws when roll%5==0 (1/5); burn/poison residual max(1,floor(maxHp/8)); burn halves physical attack; toxic max(1,floor(maxHp*counter/16)); paralysis stops when roll%4==0 (1/4); sleep wakes and can move when the counter hits 0. BADGES (Crystal, as gen1recomp src/battle/gen2/Battle.lua ports it): badgeStats is Effects.badgeBoost(stat, key, badges, spa) -> value, badges a set of Gold ids. ZEPHYR->atk, MINERAL->def, PLAIN->spe, GLACIER->spa, each boostStat = min(999, v + floor(v/8)); Kanto ids boost no stat; spd only when GLACIER is held and glacierBoostsSpDef(boostStat(spa)): true at >= 999, else a = (floor(v/256) - 3 - (v%256 < 231 ? 1 : 0)) mod 256 and boosted when a is odd. badgeTypes is Effects.badgeTypeBoost(typeId, badges) -> boosted: the first of the 16 DoBadgeTypeBoosts rows naming typeId (registry id, PSYCHIC_TYPE for Psychic) answers whether its badge is held. Damage's badgeTypeBoost adds max(1, floor(d/8)) right after the 997+2 tail and before STAB.",
